Define BUFSIZ for the freestanding grub script lexer so flex 2.6.5 works.

flex 2.6.5 changed the scanner skeleton to read in stdio-sized chunks:

    #define YY_READ_BUF_SIZE BUFSIZ

flex 2.6.4 used a fixed 8192 there. grub builds grub-core with -nostdinc,
so BUFSIZ is never declared and grub_script.yy.c stops compiling:

    grub_script.yy.c:1222:26: error: 'BUFSIZ' undeclared

yylex.l already carries "flex hacks for -nostdinc" for stdin, stdout,
fprintf and exit under #ifndef GRUB_UTIL. Add BUFSIZ there, set to the
8192 that flex 2.6.4 used, so the module build reads the same amount it
did before. GRUB_UTIL builds keep the libc value. With flex 2.6.4 the
define is unused, so the patch is safe on either version.

--- a/grub-core/script/yylex.l
+++ b/grub-core/script/yylex.l
@@ -93,6 +93,10 @@
 
 #define fprintf(...) (void)0
 #define exit(...) grub_fatal("fatal error in lexer")
+/* flex 2.6.5 reads in BUFSIZ chunks, and BUFSIZ comes from stdio.h.  */
+#ifndef BUFSIZ
+#define BUFSIZ 8192
+#endif
 #endif
 
 }
